.TH SMI-EXAMPLE-ELIXIR 1 "November 2026" "setmy.info" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
smi-example-elixir \- example of a compiled Elixir command
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-example-elixir
[\fB\-\-version\fR | \fINAME\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Greets every \fINAME\fR, or the world without one.
.TP
.B \-\-version
prints the version of the application.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ERL_LIBS
further library directories, after the ones of the package.
